    "text": "**Business & market dynamics:** The core Brand to Demand segment is gaining momentum, led by the unified demand product suite, despite a challenging macro environment. In contrast, the Intelligence & Advisory unit is contracting, largely from reduced go‑to‑market consulting. The overall picture is one of a business pivoting toward higher‑growth demand‑generation capabilities while legacy advisory work softens, and a significant goodwill impairment related to the Informa Tech combination signals a reset of asset values from the merger.\n\n**Management strategy and execution:** Leadership is focused on post‑merger simplification, cost discipline, and customer‑centric innovation. The early results show improving operational efficiency and expanding adjusted profitability. Management’s decision to reiterate full‑year guidance underscores confidence in the trajectory, even as the large non‑cash impairment dulls headline earnings. The team is steering toward a leaner, more focused organization built to strengthen its position as a growth accelerator in B2B tech.",
